Options registered as valueless (``store_true`` style), such as ``--exit-zero``,
are now honored when their ``false`` value is set in a configuration file.
Previously ``exit-zero = false`` in a config file was parsed into the command
line as ``--exit-zero False``, which argparse treats as the flag being present
(it takes no argument), silently enabling the option. The parser now drops the
``true``/``false`` value for valueless options, so ``exit-zero = false`` leaves
the flag off as the documented config-file syntax intends.

Closes #8460
